You need to configure the role assignment for User1 by using Microsoft Graph PowerShell. $user and $role already contain User1 and the User Administrator role definition.

How should you complete the script? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.

```powershell
$params = @{
  Action           = "[[1]]"
  PrincipalId      = $user.Id
  RoleDefinitionId = $role.Id
  DirectoryScopeId = "/"
  Justification    = "IT operations eligibility"
  ScheduleInfo     = @{
    StartDateTime = Get-Date
    Expiration    = @{
      Type        = "[[2]]"
      EndDateTime = [System.DateTime]::Parse("2027-06-30T00:00:00Z")
    }
  }
}
[[3]] -BodyParameter $params
```
